---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Does Yank send my clipboard anywhere?",
    a:
      "No. The local app runs the classifier and the natural-language search on your device. Sync (Pro) is opt-in and end-to-end encrypted — we can't read it either. We don't collect analytics events tied to clip content.",
    open: true,
  },
  {
    q: "How does the natural-language search actually work?",
    a:
      "Two layers. A lightweight on-device model tags each clip with a type and extracts entities (phone, date, repo, color, etc). When you ask a question, a second pass matches your phrasing against those tags, the time window you mentioned, and the source app. No round trip required.",
  },
  {
    q: "What about passwords and credit cards?",
    a:
      "Yank detects sensitive patterns — credit cards, API tokens, things that look like passwords — and either skips them entirely or stores them with a short expiry. Pro adds custom redaction rules per pattern.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will it work with my password manager / 1Password / Raycast?",
    a:
      "Yes. Yank co-exists with other tools that touch the clipboard. It respects the \"concealed\" flag password managers set, so secrets aren't archived. Raycast and Alfred users can keep their launchers; Yank only intercepts the paste flow.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is it really open-source?",
    a:
      "The local app is MIT-licensed and on GitHub. The Pro sync server is source-available — you can read it, you can self-host it, you just can't resell it.",
  },
  {
    q: "Linux support?",
    a:
      "Beta. Wayland is solid, X11 is solid, the system tray integration on KDE is still a little awkward. Help us out — issues welcome.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" data-screen-label="faq">
  <div class="wrap faq">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h2>Reasonable questions, honest answers.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      {
        faqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="q" open={item.open}>
            <summary>{item.q}</summary>
            <p class="a">{item.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
